.direnv
zig-out
.zig-cache
*.o
*.a
a.out

# Where the build unpacks a dependency it was given. The tarball it comes from
# lives in Zig's own cache outside the tree; this is the extracted copy, and a
# build recreates it from `build.zig.zon` whenever it is missing -- so what
# pins the dependency is the hash in that file, and this is an artefact of
# having built rather than part of what was written.
zig-pkg/

# tree-sitter build outputs. `grammar.js` is the source; a regenerated parser.c
# is a six-figure-line diff that makes a grammar change unreviewable, and a
# generated file in the tree can disagree with what it was generated from.
editor-support/tree-sitter-linea/src/
